---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Prose from "@/components/Prose.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Porul.in" description="Who runs Porul.in and the editorial standards behind the publication.">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="page-intro__kicker">About Porul.in</p>
      <h1>An independent publication for Tamil Nadu precision engineering.</h1>
      <p class="page-intro__dek">Porul.in exists to tell durable company stories, read sector signals, and convene a reviewed room without becoming a directory, marketplace, or sourcing desk.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-band">
    <div class="wrap page-grid">
      <Prose>
        <h2>Who Runs It</h2>
        <p>Porul.in is founder-led. The founder has final approval on every stage of the website and on the editorial standards that protect the publication's credibility.</p>
        <h2>Why It Exists</h2>
        <p>Tamil Nadu precision engineering deserves a serious public record: company stories that age well, sector intelligence that procurement people can use, and clear boundaries around what Porul.in does not do.</p>
        <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
        <p>Reporting is real, sponsorship is disclosed, and scale is never invented. Featured companies do not pay for coverage unless marked Sponsored.</p>
        <p>Porul.in does not broker, match, source, quote, or fulfil. Those boundaries are public because credibility is the product.</p>
      </Prose>
      <aside class="panel cham">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Editorial, Room, and sponsorship enquiries are read directly by the founder.</p>
        <p><a href="mailto:hello@porul.in">hello@porul.in</a></p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
